    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup optimized to exploit favorable matchups against moderate starters, led by the high-upside profile of **Jackson Merrill**. With a score of 75.27, **Jackson Merrill** is our strongest play today; his matchup against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez is bolstered by the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an elite environment for his speed-based value. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) benefits from a prime matchup against Michael Lorenzen. Despite the #8 spot in the order, the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and dynamic platoon advantages makes **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** a high-leverage start, provided the 33% rain risk in that stadium doesn't force a postponement.\n\nWe have strategically prioritized speed and platoon versatility today, though several players face tighter margins. **Nasim Nunez** (68.97) earns a spot largely due to his ability to exploit the wind and the favorable conditions against Michael Lorenzen, even from the bottom of the order. Conversely, our most difficult decision was keeping **Miguel Vargas** on the bench. While his score of 56.16 reflects strong underlying metrics\u2014specifically an excellent xwOBA of .399 and a favorable matchup against a pitcher with slow delivery\u2014he was narrowly edged out by our positional requirements and the higher raw scoring potential of our active outfielders. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that every lineup is currently \"pending.\" We are monitoring the 33% rain risk for **Curtis Mead**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** closely. Furthermore, while **Kyle Tucker** is an essential anchor for our offensive production, his score of 57.44 is suppressed by a high-stakes matchup against Zack Wheeler; we are banking on his talent floor to outweigh the elite skill of the opposing arm. We expect our active starters to maintain the necessary efficiency to stay above our performance floor, but we are prepared to pivot if official lineups significantly alter the projected order or if inclement weather forces a scratch.",
